  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Rama @ Namdeo S/O Laxman Shewale vs State Of Mah. Thr. P.S.O. P.S. Khadan, ... on 16 November, 2021 Author: Vinay Joshi Bench: V. G. Joshi Order 1611aba 1 In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Nagpur Bench : Nagpur. Criminal Application [Aba] No. 770/2021. Rama @ Namdeo Laxman Shewale -Versus- State of Maharashtra, through Khadan Police Station, Akola. Office Notes, Office Memoranda of Coram, Court's or Judge's appearances, Court's orders of directions and Registrar's orders Shri S.A. Mohta, Advocate for the Applicant. Shri H.D. Dubey, A.P.P. for the Non-applicant Coram : Vinay Joshi, J. Date : November 16, 2021 Heard. 2.",
    "facts": "3. It is submitted that the applicant is no way concerned with the alleged contraband articles. 4. Perusal of the first information report Order 1611aba770.21 indicates that in receipt of secret information, the police raided the godown and found stock of contraband material. Co-accused in the matter has stated that the contraband articles are owned by the applicant. The said statement is categorically denied by the applicant.",
    "arguments": "At this juncture, the learned Counsel for the applicant made a statement that the said crime registered with Khadan Police Station was relating to Maharashtra Rama @ Namdeo S/O Laxman Shewale vs State Of Mah. Thr. P.S.O. P.S. Khadan, ... on 16 November, 2021 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/156995507/ 1 Prevention of Gambling Act, against some third person.",
